35,2,1,talk,Minato,,"Um, I found out that our developers are very busy until the third quarter. Also, some people in the coordination group are doing a lot of work by hand because positions aren't filled. It seems a bit tiring.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"That is concerning, Minato. I found that network coverage at customer plants is quite unstable, and visitor approvals take far too long. It seems we often overlook these external dependencies when planning our timelines.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,George,,"My findings are equally concerning. The capital budget is frozen, meaning we must rely on the recurring software allowance. Furthermore, per-head licensing costs will only increase as we scale, unlike the stable fixed-fee options.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,May,,"How predictable! It turns out our ""successes"" are just the tiny tools that didn't ask too much of anyone. The big, ambitious cross-unit projects? Most just drifted away without an owner. We're repeating the same cycle, aren't we?","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Midori,,"It sounds like we are all seeing some real struggles. I found that we're losing nearly an hour every day just copying records, and misrouted deliveries are happening because different units have different addresses for the same firm.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@Midori, an hour every day sounds like a lot of time. I'm worried that if we pick a project that adds more work, the people who are already tired will have to do even more.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, I share your concern. If we ignore the instability of customer site access and the lack of developer availability, we risk promising a delivery date that is simply impossible to meet.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,George,,"@Jonathan, exactly. We must be careful not to commit to a project that looks good on paper but creates a financial burden we cannot sustain, especially with the capital budget frozen. We need a sustainable solution.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,May,,"@George, ""sustainable"" is just a fancy word for ""small,"" isn't it? If we keep picking the safe, tiny options because we're scared of the budget or the workload, we'll never actually fix anything. But then again, who wants to fail?","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I don't think it's about being scared. I just worry that we overlook the small, repetitive burdens. If we can fix those daily losses, it might actually give people the energy to try something bigger.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"I agree with @Midori. Maybe we should look for a proposal that helps people feel less tired? I'm worried that if we don't think about the staff's time, they might get too overwhelmed.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that is a gentle and thoughtful approach. If we select a proposal that simplifies existing burdens rather than adding new ones, we can avoid the stress of unrealistic deadlines and unstable external conditions.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,George,,"I agree. However, we must ensure that ""simplifying"" doesn't lead us into a trap of escalating license fees. A solution that reduces manual work but increases recurring costs is not a true victory.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're so focused on the pennies! But @Midori is right; if we just fix the annoying little things, maybe we won't be so exhausted. Still, let's not pick something that'll just vanish without an owner.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""George"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm glad we're on the same page. If we can find a proposal that addresses those daily frustrations without adding a heavy financial or workload burden, it would be a wonderful win for everyone.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I hope we can find something that makes everyone's day a little easier. I'll be thinking about the people who have to do the hard work while we decide.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I believe we have a shared understanding now. Let us look for a proposal that is realistic about our constraints and respects the time of those implementing it. I am ready to see the candidates.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,George,,I agree. Let us proceed with a clear head. We must prioritize a proposal that is financially viable within our current constraints and does not create an unsustainable long-term liability. I am ready.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,May,,"I'm ready too! Let's see if any of these candidates are actually realistic, or if we're just about to fund another project that'll be forgotten by next year. Bring them on!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I'm ready as well. I hope we can find a proposal that truly values the effort of our staff and solves those quiet, everyday problems that often go unnoticed.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
