60,3,1,talk,Minato,,"I think Proposal C, the Supplier Data Hub, sounds very helpful. @Midori mentioned that different addresses cause misrouted deliveries, so this could fix that and save people from doing the same work many times.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, that is a very observant connection. Proposal C addresses the data fragmentation Midori found. However, Proposal D's synchronization feature is also appealing, as it accounts for the network instability I discovered at customer plants.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Minato"",""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,George,,"While Proposal D is thoughtful, I am concerned about the costs of a mobile app. Proposal C seems more stable. A central repository is likely a fixed-fee effort rather than a per-head license burden.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,"@George, you're practically drooling over Proposal C! But let's be real: a ""shared update procedure"" sounds like a nightmare that'll be abandoned in six months. Still, it's better than a fancy app that crashes.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,"I agree with @Minato. Proposal C directly addresses the misrouted deliveries and the time lost to copying records. It solves those quiet, everyday frustrations and would truly make the staff's daily work much smoother.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Minato,,"@Jonathan, Proposal D sounds useful, but I'm worried about the developers. Since they are so busy until the third quarter, maybe a big app is too hard to make right now? Proposal C seems a bit kinder to them.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, you make a fair point. A complex app could lead to the same unrealistic promises we've struggled with before. Proposal C is more contained and respects our current developer constraints.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,George,,I agree. Proposal C is the most prudent choice. It addresses the operational inefficiencies Midori noted without risking the budget freezes or the escalating license costs that often plague more complex software deployments.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"@George, you're so convinced! But look, Proposal C is exactly the kind of ""cross-unit"" project that usually dies because nobody wants to own the cleanup. Still, it's the least likely to be a total disaster.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@May, I understand your worry, but if we can eliminate that hour of daily copying, people might actually have the energy to make the ownership work. It's a practical fix for a real problem.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Minato,,"I feel like we all agree that Proposal C helps the most people. I'm just a little worried about who will manage the updates, but if it stops the mistakes and the tired feeling, it's worth it.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minato, your concern is valid, but the risk of failure is lower than the risk of promising a complex app we cannot deliver. Proposal C is a realistic step that respects our current limitations.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,George,,"I agree. Proposal C is the only option that aligns with our financial constraints and operational needs. It is a sensible, sustainable choice that avoids the pitfalls of escalating costs and unrealistic timelines.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"@George, you're so boringly sensible! I'm still convinced this ""shared procedure"" is a fairy tale, but compared to the others, it's the only one that doesn't sound like a complete fantasy. I'll play along.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""George""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm so glad we can all agree. By choosing Proposal C, we're not just picking a tool, but showing the staff that we see and value the hard work they do every day.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Minato,,I'm happy that we found a way to help everyone. I will vote for Proposal C because it seems like the kindest choice for the people doing the work.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree. Proposal C is the most realistic and considerate choice, avoiding the pitfalls of unstable external conditions and overstretched resources. I will also vote for Proposal C.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,George,,"I will vote for Proposal C. It is the most fiscally responsible option, fitting within our current budget constraints without creating a long-term financial liability. It is a prudent and sustainable decision.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,"I'll vote for Proposal C too. It's probably doomed to be ignored once the novelty wears off, but it's the least offensive option here. Let's see if this one actually survives its first year!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I will also vote for Proposal C. It's a wonderful way to address the real, daily burdens our staff face. I truly believe that solving these small frustrations will bring a lot of harmony to their work.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
